Removed the separate `initialized` flag by using `lookup[0]` as the initialization sentinel and dropped the redundant null check during table construction. This saves a static load and branch on every call and simplifies the one-time initialization.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* lookup[65536] = {};

    if (lookup[0] == nullptr)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```